# CredLens - example environment variables.
#
# This file documents variable NAMES that future phases of the project may
# read from the environment. It contains no real credentials and no real
# values. Copy it to `.env` locally if/when a future phase requires it;
# `.env` itself is git-ignored and must never be committed.
#
# Nothing in this file is read by the foundation phase implemented so far.

# --- Application ---
CREDLENS_ENV=development
CREDLENS_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# --- Future: local warehouse (DuckDB / Postgres), not used yet ---
CREDLENS_DB_PATH=data/warehouse/credlens.duckdb
# CREDLENS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/credlens

# --- Kaggle API (Home Credit Default Risk source; BLOCKED_REQUIRES_USER_ACCESS
# as of Phase 2 - see docs/data_licensing.md). Only variable NAMES are listed
# here, never values. If you later set these up yourself, put real values in
# a local, git-ignored `.env` or in Kaggle's own kaggle.json - never here, and
# never in code, config/base.yaml, or a committed file of any kind.
# KAGGLE_USERNAME=
# KAGGLE_KEY=
